# Architecture Decision Records

Whenever introducing architectural changes, create or update an ADR.

Architectural changes include:

- logging
- caching
- authentication
- authorization
- messaging
- eventing
- databases
- queues
- observability
- tracing
- metrics
- deployment
- infrastructure
- api protocall
- background processing 

---

## ADR Location

Use:

```
adr/
```

---

## Naming

```
0001-title.md
0002-title.md
```

Never overwrite previous ADRs.

---

## Template

Every ADR should contain:

# Title

## Status

Accepted

## Context

## Problem

## Decision

## Alternatives Considered

## Consequences

## References

---

## Updates

If an ADR already exists for the same topic:

Update it instead of creating duplicates.

---

## Logging ADR

When introducing structlog include:

- Why structlog
- JSON logging
- Request IDs
- Event taxonomy
- Future OpenTelemetry integration